From 713bc221262ed8170be646b009ea9651cf039eb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:51:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(process): keep a sandbox job's env through the idle
 reaper and re-attach a dead poller handle

The idle reaper asked has_active_processes(<container key>), which matches the raw owner id, so a
profile-scoped Docker env (profile:<name>) was torn down ~5 min after its session went idle while a
background job still ran in it. The poller's next execute() raised and the session was told the job
ended (exit -1, lost/backend_lost) while it kept running (hub alpha-askeve proc_eb13cdee12de,
2026-10-30 12:55). The reaper now keeps any env whose container key hosts a running process, and a
poller whose handle dies re-attaches via the recorded sandbox handle (running, not restarted, wrapper
pid file present) before it reports lost.
